<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kayı tribe</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Qayı clan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kayı tribe was a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oghuz-turks">Oghuz Turks</a>. Ottoman tradition holds that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osman-i">Osman I</a>, the founder of the dynasty, belonged to the Kayı clan. The tribe is thus associated with the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> in the Bithynian borderlands.</p></div>
